# What ships is a `git archive` of a commit, and it is unpacked on Linux.
# Without this, a checkout on Windows turns every shell script and unit file
# into CRLF, and the archive carries that along -- systemd and /bin/sh both
# refuse the result. Text stays LF everywhere it matters.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
